  {
   "id": "b4",
   "function": "explanation",
   "scene_type": "zlx_cutaway",
   "spoken": "More pressure means finer droplets. According to the lecture they are ten to fifty micrometres across with direct injection, and eighty to two hundred with port injection. Inside the cylinder they have very little time to evaporate. The finer the droplets, the faster they evaporate.",
